{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792232504,"nonce":"YCGjlQFsr2lLvQndEn+BlPwSBts=","message":"Landed in 063e9a54f58c9f0fd46ee81b0198a5cd66e52c11.\n\n- Rows: a for_each keyed by visual-line index. A kept key keeps its element, so each row binds its text, colour and selection highlight (bound translate and width) to its index; rows come and go only when the count changes.\n- Placeholder: row 0 of an empty field shows it, coloured by the shared text-colour computed.\n- notify_text_area resolves the config against the stylesheet and lays the lines out again before bumping the revision, so handlers between frames see current lines. It skips the layout when a hash of the lines and sizes (laid_out, set by compute_visual_lines) is unchanged, so hover and focus do not remeasure.\n- State: revision, node_id and config replace stateful_state; TextareaRef, the focus queue, focused_text_area_node_id and both blur paths use them. refresh_text_area is the public repaint. clear_focused_text_area, which had no caller, is gone.\n- Book: the text area examples called methods that do not exist; corrected, with refresh_text_area documented.\n\nTests: tests/text_area_in_place.rs (typing and Enter, placeholder, hover and focus, a two-line selection, the caret following the cursor) asserts no subtree rebuild; all five fail against the old widget. Checked in cn_demo with synthetic input: focus ring and caret, three typed lines, a selection across two lines with the break sliver, scrolling to keep the caret in view past four rows, and a wrapped long line.","files":null}]}